{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"CodeGraph emits value-reference edges so `codegraph impact` and the impact trail in `codegraph_explore` can catch the “change this table, break its readers” case that plain calls/imports miss, especially for shared constants, lookup tables, and config values. It keeps them precise by only creating edges when the value reader can be structurally resolved, and by skipping bundled/minified files and ambiguously-shadowed names so it avoids speculative links. [CHANGELOG](https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)"}}
